\ Regression for AOT direct native wrappers.
\ Non-generic natives (dup, swap, drop) compile to their generated onez_n_
\ wrapper symbols instead of jitNativeWordCall, while a generic native (+, -)
\ keeps routing through jitNativeWordCall so generic dispatch still fires.
\ Correct output proves both paths run together under AOT.

3 dup + .       \ 6
1 2 swap - .    \ 1
4 5 6 drop + .  \ 9
2.5 dup + .     \ 5.0
